-- title:
--   Residual modularity from a proper exit ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ and let $p$ and $N$ be natural numbers with $N \neq 0$. Write $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 {n | n ∣ N}`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the Hecke generators attached to the set of divisors of $N$, and let [`ModularCurve.exitIdeal N W p`](def/ModularCurve_SupportTransfer.html#L25) be the ideal of $\mathbb{T}$ spanned by the image of $p$ in $\mathbb{T}$ together with all elements `exitGen N W ℓ` for primes $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \neq p$ and $(\ell : \mathbb{Z}) \nmid W.\Delta$. The hypothesis is that this ideal is not the unit ideal. The conclusion is `W.IsResiduallyModularOfLevel p N`: there exist a cusp form $f$ of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$ and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ of the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$ with $p \in \mathfrak{m}$, such that $f$ is a normalised eigenform in the sense of the project predicate — the $q$-expansion coefficients satisfy $a_1 = 1$, $a_{mn} = a_m a_n$ for coprime $m,n$, $a_{q^{r+2}} = a_q a_{q^{r+1}} - q\,a_{q^r}$ for primes $q \nmid N$ and $a_{q^{r+2}} = a_q a_{q^{r+1}}$ for primes $q \mid N$ — and such that for every prime $\ell$ with $(\ell : \mathbb{Z}) \nmid W.\Delta$, $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \neq p$, the coefficient $a_\ell(f)$ is the image of an algebraic integer $a$ with $a - W.\mathrm{apOfModel}(\ell) \in \mathfrak{m}$, where $W.\mathrm{apOfModel}(\ell)$ is the trace of Frobenius of the reduction of $W$ modulo $\ell$.
--
--   This is the passage from a proper "exit ideal" $(p,\ T_\ell - a_\ell(W))$ in the integral Hecke algebra of $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$, anemic away from the divisors of $N$, to the existence of a weight-$2$ normalised eigenform on $\Gamma_0(N)$ whose Hecke eigenvalues are congruent to the Frobenius traces of $W$ modulo a maximal ideal above $p$. It is the interface used when residual modularity of a given level is produced from Hecke-module information, and it feeds the deductions of residual modularity from lower-level torsion and from the level-divisibility statement.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_isResiduallyModularOfLevel_of_exitIdeal_ne_top.lean

